<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Harzgerode</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Harzgerode is a small town in the eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/harz">Harz</a> mountains of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saxony-anhalt">Saxony-Anhalt</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>. Nearby, in the Selke valley, stand the ruins of Anhalt castle, which gave its name to the principality of Anhalt. The town belonged to the Anhalt princes, later to the line of Anhalt-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bernburg">Bernburg</a>, and was a centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/silver">silver</a> and lead mining.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/harzgerode.jpg" alt="Harzgerode" width="320" height="234" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: F. Hoffmann · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Harzgerode_Markt.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
